# boardwalk — copy to .env for local runs (`go run ./cmd/examples/boardwalk`).
#
# The live game runs entirely in memory (the ecs.Store/sim), but boardwalk
# requires the full Beach stack to boot: Postgres holds the periodic CBOR
# snapshot of the store (restored on boot) and ClickHouse holds the action
# firehose behind /stats. Both DSNs are required — the binary exits with the
# missing list if either is unset. These point at a LOCAL Postgres/ClickHouse
# (e.g. ones you ran with published ports); `docker compose up` sets its own
# service-name values and does not read this file.
PORT=8080
DATABASE_URL=postgres://beach:beach@localhost:5432/boardwalk?sslmode=disable
CLICKHOUSE_DSN=clickhouse://beach:beach@localhost:9000/beach
